type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable PostgreSQL server and a role allowed to create databases and schemas"},"203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a reachable RabbitMQ broker and credentials"},"204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"an OIDC provider, normally Keycloak, with a realm/tenant and client for Lamassu"},"205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"Envoy Gateway 1.8+ and a `GatewayClass`"},"206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"cert-manager 1.14+; for trusted TLS, either a trusted issuer or a Kubernetes TLS Secret"},"207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"a StorageClass and an external traffic design"},"208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"Version-specific upgrade steps live in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` in the Helm repository. The chart also ships an optional pre-upgrade Job that migrates existing CA private keys into the KMS engine configured for the release. It is off by default (`migrations.caToKms.enabled: false`) and is only needed when upgrading from a version prior to 3.7.0."},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"While the flag is enabled, every `helm upgrade` creates the `<chart fullname>-ca-to-kms-migration` Job (`lamassu-ca-to-kms-migration` for release `lamassu`); a fresh install does not create it. It runs before the other pre-upgrade hooks, the authorization bootstrap configuration and the database-migration Job, which use hook weights `-4` and `-3` versus its `-10`."},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"The Job consumes the same KMS service configuration the chart renders into the KMS ConfigMap, including the engines from `services.kms.cryptoEngines`, and runs the migration tool defined in `migrations.caToKms.image`. It mounts that configuration read-only at `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml` from the ConfigMap key `config`, so configure the destination engine in your values before the upgrade that performs the migration."},"228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"The Job resolves its configuration through a projected volume with two optional sources: the release-scoped `<chart fullname>-kms-config` (`lamassu-kms-config` for release `lamassu`, `prod-lamassu-kms-config` for release `prod`) and the legacy unscoped `kms-config` created by chart versions before release-scoped naming. The legacy configuration remains authoritative while it is still present, and the release-scoped one is used once the legacy one is gone. Both sources are optional, so a missing ConfigMap never leaves the upgrade pod in `ContainerCreating`."},"229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#upgrading-lamassu","content":"Keep `migrations.caToKms.enabled: true` for the upgrade that performs the migration, then remove the flag from your values once the migration completes; it defaults to `false`."},"230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"the migration notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade, including the optional CA-to-KMS migration hook described above"},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"The complete values reference is maintained in `charts/lamassu/VALUES.md` in the Helm repository."},"240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"page","content":"Expose the Gateway","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking"},"241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","content":"Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways."},"242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"Expose the Lamassu Gateway"},"243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"What if you need three Gateways?"},"249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Verify the traffic path"},"251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."},"252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"External reachability is the result of the whole path. A `Gateway` resource alone does not configure your router, firewall, DNS, cloud load balancer or upstream NAT."},"253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Usually, no. If you omit it, the Gateway controller and the cluster load-balancer implementation can assign an address and report it in `Gateway.status.addresses` and the generated Service status."},"254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Set it only when:"},"255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"your cloud or bare-metal load balancer supports requesting a specific address"},"256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"that address is allocated to this Gateway"},"257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"the surrounding network already routes traffic for it to the cluster"},"258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."},"259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Keep these two settings separate:"},"260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`gateway.addresses` requests an address for the Gateway."},"261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."},"262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"If users connect by DNS name, put that name in `tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.hostnames`. Do not copy an upstream proxy's public IP into `gateway.addresses`."},"263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"For a small VM running K3s or MicroK8s, use one external Lamassu Gateway and route every Lamassu endpoint through it:"},"264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"This design uses one IP, one TLS entry point and one pair of ports. The chart already creates the required routes."},"265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."},"266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"For the recommended design:"},"267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Use only one externally exposed Lamassu Gateway."},"268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Ensure ports 80 and 443 are free. Disable or reconfigure Traefik if it is not part of your traffic path."},"269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Allow those ports through the VM firewall and any upstream security group."},"270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Point DNS at the VM's reachable address."},"271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"See the K3s ServiceLB documentation for its host-port behavior and how to replace it with another load-balancer implementation."},"272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."},"273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"An external public address can forward TCP 80 and 443 to the VM or to a Kubernetes-side VIP:"},"274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"The public IP belongs to the external device. Leave `gateway.addresses` unset or set it to the actual Kubernetes-side address, never to an address that the cluster cannot bind."},"275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"First decide whether you need three independent data planes or only three hostnames."},"276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Requirement"},"277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Recommended design"},"278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Consequence"},"279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Several Lamassu URLs or services"},"280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One Gateway with multiple routes"},"281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One IP and one proxy fleet; this is the chart default"},"282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways and separate external IPs"},"283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One VIP per Gateway"},"284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"},"285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways on one node and one IP"},"286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."},"295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway normally provisions a proxy fleet per `Gateway`. Its merged-Gateway mode can share one fleet and address, but it is not a drop-in switch for multiple Lamassu releases: the generated Lamassu listeners use the same ports and protocols without distinct hostnames, so they conflict unless you deliberately customize the listener design."},"296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"},"297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."},"298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If one Gateway can own TLS and routing, use the chart default."},"299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If Gateways need independent policy and you can allocate IPs, use one VIP per Gateway."},"300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If only the Kubernetes resources need separation, evaluate merged-Gateway mode and make every listener tuple unique."},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If data planes and TLS termination must stay independent behind one IP, add a front-door SNI passthrough layer."},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If none of those are possible, use different external ports or change the external network design."},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Check, in order:"},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"`Gateway` has `Accepted=True` and `Programmed=True`."},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Its status contains the expected address."},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The generated `LoadBalancer` Service has a usable external address."},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Port 443 reaches that address from the client network."},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"DNS resolves to the externally reachable endpoint."},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The certificate contains the DNS name or IP used by the client."},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The Gateway API treats addresses as desired state that a controller may assign or reject; see the Gateway API overview for the resource model."},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"page","content":"Kubernetes self-managed","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/overview"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/deployment/self-hosted/overview-0","page_id":"/do