url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"Current certificate revoked"},"1152":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"Renewal rejected; prepare authorized recovery according to the cause."},"1153":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"CA, profile or signing error"},"1154":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"Active CA, available key, selected profile and restrictions. Successful cacerts does not prove issuance."},"1155":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"HTTP 200 without a device connection"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"Installed pair, chain, uses, consumer trust and permissions. Also check the slot and history."},"1157":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"Timeout or error after issuance"},"1158":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#error-codes-and-diagnostics","content":"New certificates, current slot and previous identity's state before retrying."},"1159":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#compatibility-notes","content":"The examples use the contract of the examined backend. Do not automatically attribute that behavior to another release. Check the saved renewal mode after migration and Gateway behavior with expired certificates and the bootstrap CA."},"1160":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#compatibility-notes","content":"The default response is Base64-encoded DER PKCS#7; PEM through `Accept: application/x-pem-file` is a Lamassu extension. ServerKeyGen returns multipart and requires handling each part separately. See the EST reference."},"1161":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"Check HTTPS with the approved root and query cacerts for the correct APS."},"1162":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"Review the saved DMS: protocol, registration, authentication for that operation, CA, profile and window."},"1163":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"Verify the CSR locally and relate its CN to the inventory."},"1164":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"Make one request, save headers/body and query the device and certificates."},"1165":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"If you receive an identity, check the key, subject, use and connection with the consumer."},"1166":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"External bootstrap revocation checks have limitations: absence of evidence can be accepted, and OCSP Unknown does not cause the same rejection as Revoked. Do not assume a policy that rejects every uncertainty. An intermediate CA in the TLS chain does not prove that the entire chain reached the DMS validator either."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting#est-enrollment-fails","content":"For logs, networking, pods or Gateway headers, continue in Deployment troubleshooting. For identities issued, revoked or bound partially, use Renewal and recovery and Devices and identities."},"1168":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"page","content":"Trust distribution and updates","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities","Enrollment with PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","content":"Separate roots, intermediates and initial TLS trust when distributing or migrating certificates."},"1170":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Three trust relationships"},"1171":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#what-cacerts-returns","content":"What cacerts returns"},"1172":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Install the required material"},"1173":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#migrate-trust","content":"Migrate trust"},"1174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#check-the-update","content":"Check the update"},"1175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","content":"This guide is for device and consumer trust administrators. You need issuer inventory, trust-store access and an authenticated update channel. Distributing certificates is separate from choosing trusted anchors."},"1176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Relationship"},"1177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Material prepared by its owner"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Device → EST server"},"1179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Previously verified server root, chain or pin and TLS name."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"DMS → requester"},"1181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"CAs and rules authorizing initial or renewal credentials."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Consumer → device"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Operational identity roots, intermediates, validation and permissions."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#three-trust-relationships","content":"Obtaining a certificate does not automatically configure these relationships in third parties. Review the Trust model."},"1185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#what-cacerts-returns","content":"The DMS may include the available downstream TLS certificate, selected Managed CAs and enrollment CA. Selecting the issuer does not include every ancestor. The set may contain leaves, roots and intermediates, including multiple hierarchies during migration."},"1186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#what-cacerts-returns","content":"Position does not define the chain. Identify certificates by subject, issuer, AKI/SKI, signature and constraints. Download and inspect using EST client."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Keep initial EST server trust separate from identity consumer trust."},"1188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Select policy-approved roots as anchors."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Retain intermediates for chain building or presentation; do not automatically turn them into roots."},"1190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Present the leaf and required intermediates in mTLS. Normally the peer already trusts its root and does not need it sent."},"1191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Verify chain, dates, names, usages and revocation from the consumer."},"1192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#install-the-required-material","content":"Do not indiscriminately use all of `cacerts.pem` as `-CAfile`: this can expand trusted authorities, hide missing intermediates or trust a TLS leaf intended for another purpose."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#migrate-trust","content":"Before changing Enrollment CA, inventory disconnected equipment, bootstrap and operational certificates, and consumers. Distribute the new root and required intermediates; check that a cohort accepts both old and new chains."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#migrate-trust","content":"In the DMS, separate distributed CAs from `additional_validation_cas`, used for re-enrollment credentials. The inspected validator tries the enrollment CA followed by those CAs against the received leaf; accepting a multilevel chain requires checking what reaches the service and which issuer is configured."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#migrate-trust","content":"Switch issuance, renew in cohorts and compare the installed serial with the active slot. Remove previous trust once no legitimate equipment needs it and policy permits ending overlap. Follow Hierarchy and rotation for the PKI operation."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/trust-distribution#check-the-update","content":"Test an old identity allowed during overlap, a new one, an unknown chain and the result after removing old trust. Keep trust-store version, approved set, date and result. Reachable `/cacerts` establishes distribution only; it does not establish installation or acceptance across every device."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"page","content":"AWS IoT Core","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"Lamassu's connector for AWS IoT Core syncs device identities with the AWS platform, handling CA registration, Thing provisioning and certificate lifecycle automatically and event-driven."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#connector-architecture","content":"Connector architecture"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#required-iam-permissions","content":"Required IAM permissions"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#configuration-parameters","content":"Configuration parameters"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#ca-registration-in-aws-iot-core","content":"CA registration in AWS IoT Core"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#how-to-request-registration","content":"How to request registration"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#primary-account","content":"Primary Account"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#secondary-account-sni-only","content":"Secondary Account (SNI-only)"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#dms-configuration","content":"DMS configuration"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#none-mode","content":"`none` mode"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#auto-mode","content":"`auto` mode"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#jitp-mode","content":"`jitp` mode"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#device-provisioning-automatic-mode","content":"Device provisioning (automatic mode)"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#device-provisioning-jitp-mode","content":"Device provisioning (JITP mode)"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#certificate-status-synchronization","content":"Certificate status synchronization"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#forced-disconnect-on-revocation","content":"Forced disconnect on revocation"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#device-shadow-and-automation","content":"Device Shadow and automation"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#what-the-connector-writes-to-the-shadow","content":"What the connector writes to the shadow"},"1217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#aws-iot-policies","content":"AWS IoT policies"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"Lamassu's integration with AWS IoT Core bridges the PKI managed by Lamassu and AWS's connectivity platform. When a device obtains its certificate through the EST enrollment process, the connector ensures that certificate and its associated identity are recognized in AWS IoT Core without manual intervention. The result is that the device can authenticate directly to AWS with the same X.509 certificate Lamassu issued."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"From a protocol standpoint, the device authenticates to AWS IoT Core via mutual TLS (mTLS): it presents its Lamassu-issued X.509 certificate as the client certificate, and AWS IoT Core verifies the certificate chain up to the CA registered in the account. Lamassu acts as the certification authority (CA); the connector ensures that CA is registered in AWS and that the device's certificate is known to the platform before the device attempts to connect (in `auto` mode) or on its first connection (in JITP mode)."},"1221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"This document is aimed both at the PKI administrator, who needs to configure the connector and register CAs, and at the device firmware developer, who needs to understand how Things are named, how the Device Shadow works and what happens when a certificate is revoked. For the firmware developer, the most important fact is that **the AWS Thing name (ThingName) always corresponds to the Common Name (CN) of the certificate issued by Lamassu**, regardless of the provisioning mode."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#connector-architecture","content":"The AWS IoT Core connector is an independent Go process, a binary or container separate from Lamassu's core. In a monolithic deployment it is compiled by default (build tag `!noaws`) and activated with `aws_iot_manager.enabled: true` in the configuration file. In distributed deployments, it runs as its own container with access to Lamassu's CA, DMS Manager and Device Manager services over HTTP."},"1223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#connector-architecture","content":"The connector does not poll Lamassu's services periodically. Instead, it **subscribes to Lamassu's internal event bus** (AMQP or AWS SQS/SNS, configurable) and reacts to the events it cares about: CA creation or update, DMS creation or update, device identity binding, certificate status change, certificate metadata update and device metadata update. This event-driven model ensures synchronization with AWS is nearly immediate and produces no polling load."},"1224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#connector-architecture","content":"To avoid infinite loops, the connector ignores any event whose CloudEvent `source` field matches its own origin URI. This prevents the metadata writes the connector itself performs from re-triggering the same flow."},"1225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#connector-architecture","content":"When several connectors run in parallel, for example for different AWS accounts, each instance has its own `connector_id`. All metadata the connector writes to Lamassu is stored under the key `lamassu.io/iot/{connector_id}`, allowing coexistence without collisions."},"1226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#prerequisites","content":"Before enabling the connector you need an AWS account with the proper IAM permissions and the connector correctly configured. The deployment process (Docker Compose, Kubernetes or binary) is described in the deployment documentation."},"1227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-p