/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#verify-the-obtained-identity","content":"In Lamassu, open `est-device-001`. It must be created with the intended owning DMS, a current identity and the received certificate in its history. Compare the local serial with the slot; thresholds can show a renewal state rather than simply Active."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"In a second terminal, enter the same directory and run `umask 077`. Create a local server certificate and start a test consumer. This server trusts `device-root.pem` and requires a valid client identity:"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Leave it running. In the first terminal, connect using the obtained identity:"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Expect HTTP `200`. The client's trust in this local server is its self-signed `consumer.crt`; the server verifies the device against `device-root.pem`. The HTML file displays OpenSSL diagnostic information."},"1488":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"With the same server still running, test that a request without a client certificate is rejected:"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Rejection must correspond to a missing certificate at the server, not a stopped server. Stop the consumer with Ctrl+C after the test. This exercise demonstrates TLS authentication and key possession; your application must also define authorization and revocation consumption. Server options are described in openssl-s\\_server."},"1490":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Check"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Expected result"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#result-and-continuity","content":"Registration"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/plat