ki/key-management-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Lamassu also offers specific help for local integrations through **Sign locally with OpenSSL & PKCS11 tools**."},"2135":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Requiere el módulo, token y permisos del proveedor correspondiente. Comprueba que el identificador de Lamassu se corresponde con el objeto accesible desde ese módulo. La configuración del módulo pertenece al entorno del cliente o al Despliegue."},"2136":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/key-management#before-deleting-a-key","content":"Review **Related Entities** and locate CAs, certificates and validation processes that still need signatures. Revoking a CA does not remove the need to publish status during its retention period. Deleting a key does not automatically revoke its certificates either. Plan replacement and retention before using **Delete Key**; provider deletion behavior depends on the engine."},"2137":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"page","content":"Online validation with OCSP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI","Validation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp"},"2138":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Query signed status and verify the responder’s response."},"2139":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"2140":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"2141":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"2142":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate and verify a query"},"2143":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"2144":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"2145":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"OCSP queries a certificate’s status and returns a signed response. This guide is for an integrator checking what Lamassu publishes and how the consumer must verify it. For complete identity validation, follow Certificate validation."},"2146":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The responder retrieves the certificate by serial number and locates its issuing CA in the inventory. It translates persisted status as follows:"},"2147":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Record status"},"2148":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Signed response"},"2149":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`ACTIVE`"},"2150":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Good`."},"2151":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`REVOKED`"},"2152":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Revoked`, with revocation reason and timestamp."},"2153":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Other states, including `INACTIVE` and `EXPIRED`"},"2154":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"`Unknown` if the certificate and issuer can be retrieved."},"2155":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"An absent serial number causes a lookup error; it does not guarantee a signed `Unknown` response. Lookup or signing errors produce an HTTP failure. Treat that as unavailable evidence according to consumer policy."},"2156":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The issuing CA itself signs the response through its KMS-associated key. A delegated OCSP signing certificate is not used. An imported CA without a usable key cannot sign responses."},"2157":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The implementation sets `thisUpdate` approximately one day before response generation and `nextUpdate` one day after: the declared window is about 48 hours. Inspect received values and apply your freshness policy. The response reflects stored status when queried; a previously cached copy does not change upon revocation."},"2158":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The signer constructs OCSP URLs from configured VA domains and adds them to AIA. Without domains, there is no URL to add; an imported certificate retains its original extensions. Inspect the actual certificate:"},"2159":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Check that the consumer can reach this URL. DNS, endpoint exposure and domain configuration belong to Deployment. Changing configuration does not modify already signed certificates."},"2160":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The service accepts:"},"2161":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Method"},"2162":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"VA service path"},"2163":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Format"},"2164":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST`"},"2165":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp`"},"2166":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request, `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"2167":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET`"},"2168":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`/ocsp/{ocsp_request}`"},"2169":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"DER request encoded using padded URL Base64."},"2170":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Use POST to avoid client encoding differences. A successful response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and a DER body. The public prefix depends on the Gateway; use the URL published in the certificate and checked by the operator."},"2171":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"You need OpenSSL 3.x, `device.crt`, its direct issuer’s certificate `issuer.pem` and the consumer’s trusted roots in `roots.pem`. For an intermediate issuer, also prepare `intermediates.pem` containing the intermediate CAs."},"2172":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Generate the request:"},"2173":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"This example omits the nonce because the responder does not echo it. Verification relies on signature, response correspondence and timestamps; it does not demonstrate freshness through a nonce."},"2174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Replace the example URL with the inspected endpoint:"},"2175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"Verify the returned DER:"},"2176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#generate-and-verify-a-query","content":"For intermediates, add `-verify_other intermediates.pem`. Require successful response verification and inspect the status corresponding to `device.crt`, issuer, serial, `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate`. `Response verify OK` validates the response only: also observe `good`, `revoked` or `unknown`. Do not accept an identity based only on the command’s exit code."},"2177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"**OCSP Check** shows what Lamassu returns for a selected certificate. Complete the check from the consumer’s network and trust store: a console query does not establish its validation configuration."},"2178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"To check a change, save an earlier response, revoke a test certificate and request another response. The new query should reflect persisted status; compare timestamps to rule out reuse of an earlier response. If it fails, follow PKI troubleshooting."},"2179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960: OCSP."},"2180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"OpenSSL: openssl-ocsp."},"2181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"CRL service\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"2182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate validation\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-validation\" />"},"2183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"page","content":"PKI","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview"},"2184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","content":"Administer keys and authorities, define issuance and verify the resulting certificates."},"2185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Start here"},"2186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"What you need"},"2187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#core-capabilities","content":"Core capabilities"},"2188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Build your trust hierarchy"},"2189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Protect cryptographic keys"},"2190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue and control certificates"},"2191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Publish validation status"},"2192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"How to check the result"},"2193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#continue","content":"Continue"},"2194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","content":"The PKI section explains how to build and operate X.509 trust in Lamassu: which authorities issue, which rules apply and how to check certificates. It is intended for PKI administrators and anyone who needs to use certificates in a consuming system."},"2195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Follow PKI getting started to create a CA, issue a client certificate and verify it with OpenSSL. The result is a certificate, its private key and a verified chain."},"2196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"You can complete that path before managing devices. When you need to associate the identity with an inventory or automate its enrollment, continue in IoT Fleets."},"2197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"An accessible instance and permission to manage the keys, CAs and certificates you will use."},"2198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"An available cryptographic engine to keep the authority's key."},"2199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"The certificate's purpose, such as authenticating a client through mTLS."},"2200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"Consumer requirements: accepted issuers, algorithms, names and permitted usages."},"2201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#what-you-need","content":"Prepare the instance and cryptographic provider in Deployment. The trust model explains hierarchy choices."},"2202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Authorities sign certificates. A root establishes the trust anchor, and an intermediate separates issuance by environment or purpose. Hierarchy and rotation explains how to maintain trust when replacing an authority."},"2203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"CA signing keys are managed through KMS and cryptographic engines. A client that generates a CSR can keep its own key: preserve that custody when choosing the issuance method."},"2204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"A profile establishes subject, validity, usage and key restrictions. The CA applies issuance configuration and signs the certificate. In the inventory, you can inspect the result, download it and manage its status."},"2205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Validation covers the chain, validity, usages and revocation status. Lamassu publishes status through OCSP and CRL; the consumer configures which issuers it recognizes and how it checks that status."},"2206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"An active certificate in the console is one part of the check. Also verify that:"},"2207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its subject and extensions identify the expected client;"},"2208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview#how-to-check-the-result","content":"its public key matches the client's private key;"},"2209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-45/platform/pki/overvie