p to an EC2 instance inside your account. You keep control of the network, storage and operation of the machine."],[2053,"The backend also provides adapters for **Key Vault Keys** and **Key Vault Secrets**. The former delegates signing to the key service; the latter stores private material as secrets and signs using that material. These are different custody models. Confirm which adapter is enabled in your installation and test the required operations."],[676,"The backend applies auditing to mutations of:"],[790,"The backend saves **Decommissioned** and attempts to revoke the active version’s certificate with `CessationOfOperation` if the slot was not expired or revoked. It does not traverse all history. Deferred revocation can fail after retirement is saved; check the result by serial."],[861,"The blocks are independent:"],[996,"The body is **MIME multipart/mixed**, with the boundary specified in `Content-Type`. It contains two parts:"],[1929,"The CA hierarchy defines which authorities can sign. A root CA establishes the anchor of trust; intermediate CAs separate operating domains and avoid using the root for every issuance."],[1334,"The CA must be registered in AWS in Primary Account mode (SNI-only mode does not support JITP)."],[2241,"The CA name becomes its `Common Name`. Keep the CA usages needed to sign certificates and CRLs."],[2235,"The CA private key is used through the engine. In this path, you will download only the authority's public certificate."],[2291,"The CA rejects issuance"],[719,"The CA service issues certificates and maintains the relationship with its authority. The DMS applies the enrollment rules and exposes the EST flows so a device can request or renew an identity."],[1889,"The CA signs the CSR. The issuance profile determines the validity, uses, subject, allowed extensions and cryptographic constraints."],[2009,"The CA view lets you inspect and download the available list. Compare version, issuer and timestamps with the copy downloaded from