affic path"],[1805,"Verify these criteria together:"],[57,"Version upgrades."],[225,"Version-specific upgrade steps live in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` in the Helm repository. The chart also ships an optional pre-upgrade Job that migrates existing CA private keys into the KMS engine configured for the release. It is off by default (`migrations.caToKms.enabled: false`) and is only needed when upgrading from a version prior to 3.7.0."],[2030,"View details"],[2321,"We use `Acme Evaluation Root CA` and `device-001` as example names. If you replace them, keep the same client identifier in the steps you want to connect."],[874,"Webhook and combined modes also execute during re-enrollment when configured in its block. They do not implicitly degrade to NO\\_AUTH. An absent or unrecognized mode fails."],[800,"Webhook contract"],[612,"Webhook delivery rules"],[1129,"Webhook denies, times out or responds without authorization"],[1739,"What a profile controls"],[657,"What an event contains"],[1171,"What cacerts returns"],[1920,"What can be issued"],[80,"What Fastlane adds"],[248,"What if you need three Gateways?"],[322,"What it installs"],[1599,"What it prepares or checks"],[1397,"What it represents"],[1216,"What the connector writes to the shadow"],[2017,"What the KMS solves"],[315,"What the Lamassu chart provides"],[85,"What the script configures"],[51,"What the service manages"],[1043,"What to check"],[1120,"What to check"],[2343,"What to inspect"],[2290,"What to review"],[1574,"What you manage"],[1823,"What you must maintain"],[2186,"What you need"],[1886,"What you should watch"],[1314,"When `primary_account` is `false`, the connector registers the CA using `CertificateMode: SNI_ONLY`. This mode requires no verification code or access to the CA's private key, so it is the right choice when the CA is managed from another AWS account or when the administrator does not hold the private key. It is the usual method to register the same CA in several AWS accounts simultaneously."